    'ledger_audit_reports_title' => 'Account books, activity log, and company reports',
    'ledger_audit_reports_w1' => 'Do not turn off the activity log.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_w2' => 'Do not delete account book entries to hide a mistake. Add a new entry that corrects it.',
    'ledger_audit_reports_why' => 'Without checking the activity log, permission and money changes can go unnoticed.',
    'navigation_workspace_badge' => 'Menu, language & theme',
    'navigation_workspace_o1' => 'You can reach every section you are allowed to use from the sidebar, without guessing web addresses.',
    'navigation_workspace_o2' => 'Your theme and language stay the same as you move between pages.',
    'navigation_workspace_purpose' => 'This chapter explains the menu and screen layout, so you can find every feature without remembering web addresses.',
    'navigation_workspace_s1' => 'Use the groups in the left menu (such as Orders & delivery, Partner money, Products & stock, Reports, Settings; what you see depends on your role). Dealers and sub-dealers see New order, My orders, My money, Contact the office and so on.',
    'navigation_workspace_s2' => 'Open a main group to see the pages inside it. The page you are on is highlighted. One click opens a page quickly, without reloading everything.',
    'navigation_workspace_s3' => 'Owners and staff see Products, Stock and Branches under Products & stock. Area codes (place codes) are under Settings and Branch sales is under Reports.',
    'navigation_workspace_s4' => 'Dealers see Team members and Ranks under My team. Sub-dealers see Salary & tour instead.',
    'navigation_workspace_s5' => 'Switch language with EN / বাংলা. Labels, the manual, and many notices follow the language you choose.',
    'navigation_workspace_s6' => 'Use the Day / Night button for a light or dark screen. Your choice is saved in this browser for all Madina panels.',
    'navigation_workspace_s7' => 'Owners and staff can use the branch selector (when branches exist) to see stock and deliveries for one branch.',
    'navigation_workspace_s8' => 'Open Office notices under Contact the office to read company notices. Your own updates are under the bell icon.',
    'navigation_workspace_summary' => 'Use the sidebar groups, search Help, and change language or theme without losing your place.',
    'navigation_workspace_t1' => 'If a section is missing, you probably do not have permission for it. The link is not broken.',
    'navigation_workspace_t2' => 'On mobile the sidebar is hidden. Tap the menu button to open it.',
    'navigation_workspace_title' => 'Menu, sections, language, and theme',
    'navigation_workspace_w1' => 'Clearing browser data resets your theme and language. Day mode comes back as the default.',
    'navigation_workspace_why' => 'Madina puts many pages into groups that open and close. Knowing this map means fewer “feature missing” support requests.',
    'network_genealogy_badge' => 'Network & team',
    'network_genealogy_o1' => 'New partners are linked to the right referrer\'s code.',
    'network_genealogy_o2' => 'You can guide your team using up-to-date lists you download.',
    'network_genealogy_o3' => 'Rank progress is shown next to your team\'s health.',
    'network_genealogy_purpose' => 'The team tree drives referral commissions, rank qualification, and the leader\'s view of the team.',
    'network_genealogy_s1' => 'Open My team → Team members to copy your referral code and share the Join Poster or QR code.',
    'network_genealogy_s10' => 'If you suspect someone has opened fake extra accounts, report it to Support with proof.',
    'network_genealogy_s2' => 'Send interested people to the official join form on the website, with your code already filled in.',
    'network_genealogy_s3' => 'Check how deep your team goes and who is active.',
    'network_genealogy_s4' => 'Use filters or search when the list is long.',
    'network_genealogy_s5' => 'Download the list (CSV) when you need it for offline training.',
    'network_genealogy_s6' => 'Check Ranks along with Network to see your qualification progress.',
    'network_genealogy_s7' => 'Staff/owner: use the "Who joined under whom" page when checking support requests, and record any change of referrer as per company rules.',
    'network_genealogy_s8' => 'Never collect a new member\'s password. They create their own login.',
    'network_genealogy_s9' => 'Check that new members appear under the right referrer within the expected time.',
    'network_genealogy_summary' => 'Invite partners with your code or QR, watch your team, and download lists.',
    'network_genealogy_t1' => 'Use one official invite link per campaign so tracking stays clear.',
    'network_genealogy_t2' => 'Referral commission is paid only on orders that are fully paid and delivered: :referral_rate% to the direct referrer, :gen2_rate% to the referrer one level above and :gen3_rate% to the one above that.',
    'network_genealogy_t3' => 'Area dealer rules affect sales areas. They are not the same as the referral team tree.',
    'network_genealogy_title' => 'Network, referrals, and team tree',
    'network_genealogy_w1' => 'Changing a referrer without permission is recorded in the activity log. It is not an informal favour.',
    'network_genealogy_w2' => 'Do not sell “top positions” against company rules.',
    'network_genealogy_why' => 'Broken referral links or reused codes cause commission disputes that cannot be undone, so handle invites carefully.',
    'notifications_circulars_badge' => 'Notices & circulars',
    'notifications_circulars_o1' => 'You have a dated record of company instructions that affect your earnings and orders.',
    'notifications_circulars_o2' => 'Important unread notices are read and cleared on purpose, not ignored.',
    'notifications_circulars_purpose' => 'Company notices replace WhatsApp-only instructions for payment times, price changes, and rules.',
    'notifications_circulars_s1' => 'Press the bell for your own alerts (order status, payment updates, support replies). Partners also have them on the My updates tab under Contact the office → Office notices.',
    'notifications_circulars_s2' => 'Partners: open Contact the office → Office notices for company-wide rules and campaign messages.',
    'notifications_circulars_s3' => 'Mark a notice as read once you understand what you need to do.',
    'notifications_circulars_s4' => 'Only open links in notices that go to Madina panels or the official company website.',
    'notifications_circulars_s5' => 'Owners/staff: publish circulars from the Website/Content section with a clear start date.',
    'notifications_circulars_s6' => 'If someone gives you spoken instructions that differ from a circular, send a support request with the circular number.',
    'notifications_circulars_summary' => 'Read daily alerts, rule circulars, and account notices in one place.',
    'notifications_circulars_t1' => 'Pin or screenshot circulars about payment deadlines for your shop staff.',
    'notifications_circulars_t2' => 'A notice shows in your chosen language when a translation is available.',
    'notifications_circulars_title' => 'Notifications and company circulars',
    'notifications_circulars_w1' => 'Treat any unexpected “urgent payment” message from outside the panel as a scam until it is checked.',
    'notifications_circulars_why' => 'If you miss a circular, your withdrawal or payment may be rejected after a rule changes.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_badge' => 'Special benefits fund',
    'owner_benefits_fund_o1' => 'The owner can explain how much benefit money is left for any period.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_o2' => 'Staff panels do not show this fund.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_o3' => 'The owner\'s figures can always be matched with the company share in the company fund.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_purpose' => 'Owners need a private view of the money left over after network payments, without showing it to staff or partners.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s1' => 'Open Company accounts → Special benefits fund.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s2' => 'Filter by period to see the shares linked to each order.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s3' => 'Check each line\'s order number and net share.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s4' => 'Match it with the company share shown in the company fund.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s5' => 'Keep downloaded files offline, in storage that only owners control.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s6' => 'Do not give staff permission for this section.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s7' => 'If you see unexpected access attempts, check the Activity log.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_s8' => 'Discuss any problem only in closed meetings with owners and accounts.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_summary' => 'A private, owner-only account book of the company share left after network payments.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_t1' => 'Look at the Special benefits fund together with Branch performance for the full picture.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_t2' => 'Write down every manual correction, with legal or accounts approval.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_title' => 'Special benefits fund (company commission benefits fund)',
    'owner_benefits_fund_w1' => 'Never share screenshots of this fund in staff or partner chats.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_w2' => 'Do not treat this fund as a marketing fund for partners.',
    'owner_benefits_fund_why' => 'If this screen leaks, it causes internal conflict. The figures must still be correct for the owner\'s reports.',
    'payment_claims_badge' => 'Sending payment',
    'payouts_settlements_badge' => 'Payments & month-end',
    'payouts_settlements_o1' => 'Each payment can be traced from request → approval → payment reference.',
    'payouts_settlements_o2' => 'Month-end payment totals match the account book totals.',
    'payouts_settlements_o3' => 'Partners see their updated withdrawal and payment history after accounts marks a payment as paid.',
    'payouts_settlements_purpose' => 'Every payment from the company needs a method, a reference and a receipt, and should be checked by a second person.',
    'payouts_settlements_s1' => 'Open Partner money → Withdrawal requests to see the requests that are waiting.',
    'payouts_settlements_s10' => 'Keep month-end payment reports with the month-end file.',
    'payouts_settlements_s2' => 'Before marking paid, check that the receiving account matches the partner\'s profile and NID check.',
    'payouts_settlements_s3' => 'Mark it paid only after you send the money. Choose the method (cash, bank, bKash, Nagad or other) and enter the reference or, for cash, who took the money. The system makes a numbered receipt.',
    'payouts_settlements_s4' => 'Open Month closing to share out the dealer salary and the monthly royalty for the month that has ended.',
    'payouts_settlements_s5' => 'Each month closes on its own. Money for a target someone missed goes to the company profit fund, with the reason recorded. Only the rank award fund, the sub-dealer tour fund and the bike/car fund carry over.',
    'payouts_settlements_s6' => 'Record month-end payments only when live money records are turned on.',
    'payouts_settlements_s7' => 'Tell partners when they are paid; their history should update.',
    'payouts_settlements_s8' => 'Look into pending items that have waited longer than the agreed time.',
    'payouts_settlements_s9' => 'Owners: check a few payments at random every week.',
    'payouts_settlements_summary' => 'Pay partner withdrawals and handle month-end salary, rank bonus, and reward payments.',
    'payouts_settlements_t1' => 'When two accounts staff are available, one prepares the payment and the other approves it. Spending from company funds always needs a second person to approve.',
    'payouts_settlements_t2' => 'Keep salary payment dates in line with circulars.',
    'payouts_settlements_t3' => 'Keep tax papers with the payment receipts.',
    'payouts_settlements_title' => 'Withdrawal requests, month closing, salary, and rewards',
    'payouts_settlements_w1' => 'Do not mark a payment as paid before the bank or mobile banking transfer is done.',
    'payouts_settlements_w2' => 'Never pay using cash collected by a partner unless it is recorded in the company fund.',
    'payouts_settlements_why' => 'Paying the wrong wallet or paying twice destroys trust and makes records impossible to check.',
    'place_codes_admin_badge' => 'Place code setup',
    'place_codes_admin_o1' => 'All areas where the company sells have complete codes.',
    'place_codes_admin_o2' => 'Every partner is linked to a valid code.',
    'place_codes_admin_purpose' => 'A clean list of area codes keeps area dealer rules and reports correct.',
    'place_codes_admin_s1' => 'Open Settings → Area codes (place codes).',
    'place_codes_admin_s2' => 'Go through Division / District / Upazila / Union / Pourashava.',
    'place_codes_admin_s3' => 'Add codes with clear names. The form can add the MNHC- start for you.',
    'place_codes_admin_s4' => 'Link partners to codes when they join or when you edit their account.',
    'place_codes_admin_s5' => 'Turn off old codes instead of reusing them for new places.',
    'place_codes_admin_s6' => 'Check the changes after updating many codes at once.',
    'place_codes_admin_s7' => 'After big changes, check the Area dealers page too.',
    'place_codes_admin_s8' => 'Publish a circular when many areas are changed.',
    'place_codes_admin_summary' => 'Create and keep up the Bangladesh area codes used for joining and sales areas.',
    'place_codes_admin_t1' => 'Keep a spreadsheet list of all areas as a backup.',
    'place_codes_admin_t2' => 'After adding Bangla names, test that search finds them.',
    'place_codes_admin_title' => 'Place code setup',
    'place_codes_admin_w1' => 'Do not rename codes already printed on partner ID cards without a plan to update the cards.',
    'place_codes_admin_w2' => 'Do not give the same exclusive area to two partners.',
    'place_codes_admin_why' => 'Duplicate or unused codes quietly link sales to the wrong person.',
    'profile_security_badge' => 'Profile & security',
    'profile_security_o1' => 'Your profile shows the same details used on invoices and ID cards.',
    'profile_security_o2' => 'Unknown logins are signed out, and you change your password if you think someone knows it.',
    'profile_security_o3' => 'Two-step login (2FA) is turned on when company rules require it.',
    'profile_security_purpose' => 'Your profile details are used on invoices, ID cards, payment accounts, and sales area. Security settings stop others from reaching your wallet.',
    'profile_security_s1' => 'Open Profile and check your full name, shop name, phone, email, and address as registered with the company.',
    'profile_security_s10' => 'Log out on shared computers when you finish.',
    'profile_security_s2' => 'Check your place code and sales area when shown. They affect area dealer rules and area reports.',
    'profile_security_s3' => 'Download your Partner ID Card PDF and Join Poster from Profile, when available, to bring in new members.',
    'profile_security_s4' => 'Open Security to change your password. Use a new password that you do not use anywhere else.',
    'profile_security_s5' => 'Check your logged-in devices and sign out any you do not know right away.',
    'profile_security_s6' => 'If two-step login (2FA) is on for staff, set it up and keep the recovery codes safe offline.',
    'profile_security_s7' => 'Change payment account details only in the profile or payment fields, never by chat message.',
    'profile_security_s8' => 'After an identity correction that needs staff approval, wait until your status is Active before big orders or payments.',
    'profile_security_s9' => 'Owners/staff: keep your staff profile separate from your partner account, even when both dashboards are linked.',
    'profile_security_summary' => 'Keep your shop details correct and protect your account with a password, device checks, and two-step login (2FA) if needed.',
    'profile_security_t1' => 'Upload photos of your NID or birth certificate only through the official joining form.',
    'profile_security_t2' => 'Share your Join Poster QR only in your own recruiting channels, so codes do not get mixed up.',
    'profile_security_t3' => 'Contact Support if Profile fields are locked. Partners cannot change all NID details themselves.',
    'profile_security_title' => 'Profile, identity documents, and security',
    'profile_security_w1' => 'Staff must never ask partners for their passwords when helping them.',
    'profile_security_w2' => 'Do not email scanned NID copies. Upload them only in the panel.',
    'profile_security_why' => 'A wrong phone or email stops OTP codes and notices from reaching you. Staying logged in on shared devices is a common way fraud happens in partner networks.',
    'ranks_royalties_badge' => 'Ranks, award & royalty',
    'ranks_royalties_o1' => 'You know your current rank and what is still needed for the next one.',
    'ranks_royalties_o2' => 'You know the two kinds of rank money: a one-time award and a monthly royalty.',
    'ranks_royalties_o3' => 'Leaders can plan training around the next rank target that can be measured, not rumours.',
    'ranks_royalties_purpose' => 'Ranks reward steady buying and a strong team. Each month the rank royalty fund (:royalty_rate% of every purchase) is shared among the dealers at each rank who kept their rank that month. You get royalty only for your latest rank.',
    'ranks_royalties_s1' => 'Open Ranks, or press “See my progress” in the Targets box on the Dashboard, to see your rank and what is left for the next one.',
    'ranks_royalties_s2' => 'The ranks: Marketing Officer (MO), Area Manager (AM), Sales Manager (SM), Marketing Executive (ME).',
    'ranks_royalties_s3' => 'MO counts your own purchases. AM, SM and ME count active dealers at the needed rank in your team (see the tips below).',
    'ranks_royalties_s4' => 'The one-time rank award is paid as soon as you reach a rank. If you reach MO and then AM in the same month, you get both awards.',
    'ranks_royalties_s5' => 'Staff: see rank rules under Commission rules. Do not give ranks by hand.',
    'ranks_royalties_s6' => 'Plan training around the next target you can measure, not around titles.',
    'ranks_royalties_s7' => 'Check ranks again after months with big deliveries.',
    'ranks_royalties_s8' => 'If there is a dispute, note the month and download the “All records together” tab of My money as proof.',
    'ranks_royalties_s9' => 'At month closing, if nobody qualifies at a rank, that rank\'s royalty goes to the company profit fund.',
    'ranks_royalties_summary' => 'Follow your progress from MO → AM → SM → ME, your one-time rank awards and your monthly royalty.',
    'ranks_royalties_t1' => 'MO: your own total purchases since you joined must reach :mo_target (one-time award :mo_bonus). AM: :am_count active dealers at MO or higher within :rank_depth levels of your team (award :am_bonus). SM: :sm_count at AM or higher (award :sm_bonus). ME: :me_count at SM or higher (award :me_bonus).',
    'ranks_royalties_t2' => 'In training, keep your own retail sales separate from your team\'s sales.',
    'ranks_royalties_t3' => 'To get royalty for your rank in a month, buy at least that rank\'s monthly amount in the same month: MO :mo_keep, AM :am_keep, SM :sm_keep, ME :me_keep. For the first :grace_days days after you reach a rank, you get it even without this.',
    'ranks_royalties_title' => 'Ranks, rank awards and monthly royalty',
    'ranks_royalties_w1' => 'Do not put earlier dates on orders to make it look like you qualify.',
    'ranks_royalties_w2' => 'Staff must not give ranks by hand outside the approved tools.',
    'ranks_royalties_why' => 'Partners often mistake a one-time jump in sales for steady qualification. Ranks follow fixed rules and dates.',
    'reports_badge' => 'Reports',
    'reports_o1' => 'You have a dated copy for your monthly review.',
    'reports_o2' => 'Every figure can be traced back to the orders behind it.',
    'reports_purpose' => 'Reports add up orders, payments, and commission types. They do not change any balance.',
    'reports_s1' => 'Open the “All records together” tab of My money (dealers and sub-dealers) or Reports → Report Centre (staff) and choose a date button or your own from/to dates.',
    'reports_s2' => 'Check the number and value of orders, the payment summary, and commission totals by type.',
    'reports_s3' => 'Dealers can open the team/network parts for more detail, when shown.',
    'reports_s4' => 'Download a PDF to share with your accountant.',
    'reports_s5' => 'Staff: run company reports by Bangladesh time.',
    'reports_s6' => 'Pick one order from the report and check it against the order details.',
    'reports_s7' => 'Save the monthly PDFs as your shop\'s month-end file.',
    'reports_s8' => 'If the PDF text looks wrong, download it once more. If it is still wrong, send a support request with your browser name.',
    'reports_summary' => 'Choose dates and download PDFs for reviews and your records.',
    'reports_t1' => 'When you pick your own dates, let the last date run to the end of the day (Bangladesh time).',
    'reports_t2' => 'To compare one month with another, use the same date buttons.',
    'reports_title' => 'Business reports and the partner full report',
    'reports_w1' => 'Do not edit downloaded PDFs and show them as system originals in a dispute.',
    'reports_why' => 'An empty date range just means nothing happened in that time. The system is not down.',
    'rewards_milestones_badge' => 'Target rewards',
    'rewards_milestones_o1' => 'Progress counts only eligible sales.',
    'rewards_milestones_o2' => 'Reward payments are recorded in the month-closing pages.',
    'rewards_milestones_purpose' => 'Long-term rewards keep leaders going beyond monthly commissions.',
    'rewards_milestones_s1' => 'Partners: press “See my progress” on the Dashboard to see each target. Staff: open Commissions & rewards → Car & bike rewards. Team sales needed now: bike :bike_target, car :car_target.',
    'rewards_milestones_s2' => 'Only orders that are fully paid and delivered count, from your whole team since the start. Each direct line counts up to a limit: :bike_cap for the bike, :car_cap for the car.',
    'rewards_milestones_s3' => 'The bike/car fund is not lost at month end. It carries over from month to month.',
    'rewards_milestones_s4' => 'Staff: pay rewards from Spending from funds. Record the method and reference so a receipt is made.',
    'rewards_milestones_s5' => 'Keep award or payment circulars with your records.',
    'rewards_milestones_s6' => 'Check the progress bar and eligible sales before asking Support.',
    'rewards_milestones_s7' => 'Owners: keep the money for rewards owed separate from daily running cash.',
    'rewards_milestones_summary' => 'Follow bike, car, and other rewards against your checked target sales.',
    'rewards_milestones_t1' => 'Take photos of award receipts for your records.',
    'rewards_milestones_t2' => 'Reward items are separate from the wallet cash you can withdraw.',
    'rewards_milestones_title' => 'Rewards and sales targets',
    'rewards_milestones_w1' => 'Do not promise unfinished targets to others as guaranteed money.',
    'rewards_milestones_why' => 'Only checked and paid sales count; spoken promises do not.',
    'staff_fulfillment_badge' => 'Order approval & delivery',
    'staff_fulfillment_o1' => 'Approved orders can be paid and delivered.',
    'staff_fulfillment_o2' => 'The sending branch matches the stock movement.',
    'staff_fulfillment_o3' => 'Checked payments show on the order.',
    'staff_fulfillment_purpose' => 'This work turns partner orders into delivered goods and correctly recorded cash.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s1' => 'Open the Orders list and filter by “waiting for approval”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s10' => 'Match the value of goods sent each day with the company fund collections.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s2' => 'Check the items, prices, and partner status before you approve or reject.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s3' => 'Open Check order payments. Check the amount, method, screenshot and receiving account against the company\'s payment accounts.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s4' => 'Mark a payment as checked only when the money has really arrived.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s5' => 'Choose the delivery branch when more than one branch is in use.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s6' => 'Send the goods from Deliveries. Record the courier name and the tracking number.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s7' => 'Approve an order only when the checked payments equal the order total.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s8' => 'If fewer goods were sent, correct it with a written note as per company rules.',
    'staff_fulfillment_s9' => 'Report suspicious repeated small payments to a senior.',
    'staff_fulfillment_summary' => 'Approve orders after full payment, then send the goods.',
    'staff_fulfillment_t1' => 'Later, use Branch performance to see each branch\'s profit.',
    'staff_fulfillment_t2' => 'Write rejection reasons politely and say what the partner should do next.',
    'staff_fulfillment_title' => 'Order delivery: payment check, approval and sending',
    'staff_fulfillment_w1' => 'When company rules require it, do not approve orders from your own linked dealer account without a second person checking.',
    'staff_fulfillment_w2' => 'Never skip payment checks “as a favour”.',
    'staff_fulfillment_why' => 'Approving without checking payment, or sending from the wrong branch, breaks the stock count and the records.',
    'staff_people_accounts_badge' => 'Staff & permissions',
    'staff_people_accounts_o1' => 'Every staff member has only the permissions they need.',
    'staff_people_accounts_o2' => 'Partner joining papers are saved with the account.',
    'staff_people_accounts_o3' => 'Two-dashboard access is given on purpose and can be removed.',
    'staff_people_accounts_purpose' => 'This part controls who can do what in the system and which permissions they get.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s1' => 'Open Staff → Staff list to add staff and set their permissions (orders, accounts, stock, content, activity log, and so on).',
    'staff_people_accounts_s10' => 'Tell people about approvals through the panel status, not only by phone.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s11' => 'Owners: check the list of staff permissions from time to time.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s2' => 'Open Dealers & sub-dealers → Dealer list to search dealers, see their status, and keep their codes and areas correct.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s3' => 'Open Sub-dealer list to work with sub-dealers.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s4' => 'Handle partnership applications: check the papers, then approve or reject with a reason.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s5' => 'Give a partner staff access only after formal approval.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s6' => 'Check the activity log after changing permissions.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s7' => 'Before creating an account, check that the phone and email are not already in use.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s8' => 'Suspend an account that may be hacked before you look into it.',
    'staff_people_accounts_s9' => 'Before adding a new partner, plan the place code for their sales area.',
    'staff_people_accounts_summary' => 'Add staff, manage dealer and sub-dealer accounts, and handle partnership applications.',
    'staff_people_accounts_t1' => 'Write shop names the same way every time so search works well.',
    'staff_people_accounts_t2' => 'Check permissions again on the same day a person\'s role changes.',
    'staff_people_accounts_t3' => 'Keep the emergency owner login details sealed and stored offline.',
    'staff_people_accounts_title' => 'Staff and accounts: employees, partners, and joining',
    'staff_people_accounts_w1' => 'Never let several people share one staff login.',
    'staff_people_accounts_w2' => 'Do not approve an NID check without clear document photos.',
    'staff_people_accounts_why' => 'Staff with too many permissions and incomplete NID checks are the biggest daily risks.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_badge' => 'Salary & tour fund',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_o1' => 'You can see how much salary you have earned this month that is not yet paid.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_o2' => 'Paid amounts match the accounts month-end closing.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_o3' => 'The tour fund is not mixed up with cash you can withdraw right away.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_purpose' => 'Sub-dealers get :sub_salary_rate% salary on every purchase that is fully paid and delivered, with no minimum purchase. Another :sub_tour_rate% is saved in their own tour fund. The salary goes into the wallet after the month ends; the office uses the tour fund for company tours.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s1' => 'Open Salary & tour in the menu to see salary earned but not yet paid, and the month-end status.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s2' => 'Every purchase that is fully paid and delivered counts toward your salary. There is no minimum amount.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s3' => 'When shown, track the tour fund balance separately from your available commission wallet.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s4' => 'After month-end closing, check that the money shows in your earnings or wallet.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s5' => 'Dealers with sub-dealers: help them plan their sales. Do not lend personal cash against future salary.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s6' => 'Staff: run month-end salary from the sub-dealer pay pages and lock the month afterwards.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s7' => 'Match salary lines with the orders behind them.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s8' => 'Send a support request if month-end salary is recorded but does not match your delivered sales.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_s9' => 'Your tour fund carries over from month to month. It does not reset when a month closes.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_summary' => 'Understand the monthly salary and the tour fund that come from your purchases.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_t1' => 'Keep your invoices. Each paid and delivered order adds to that month\'s salary.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_t2' => 'Watch circulars for short-term salary offers or changes.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_title' => 'Sub-dealer salary and tour fund',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_w1' => 'The tour fund is not cash to withdraw. The office uses it to send you on company tours.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_w2' => 'Staff must not change salary percentages outside Commission rules & rates.',
    'subdealer_salary_tour_why' => 'Only orders that are fully paid and delivered count. If an order is later refunded, the salary on it is taken back.',
    'support_badge' => 'Help & support',
    'support_o1' => 'Most “how do I” questions are answered without waiting.',
    'support_o2' => 'Requests you send have enough detail for staff to check the problem.',
    'support_purpose' => 'Help yourself first to avoid delays. When a person must step in, a support request keeps a record.',
    'support_s1' => 'Open Help and search a word (order, withdrawal, branch, commission, and so on).',
    'support_s2' => 'In each chapter, read the purpose, why it matters, the steps, results, tips, and warnings.',
    'support_s3' => 'If a page stops you, follow the “finish these steps first” message and complete the earlier steps.',
    'support_s4' => 'Restart the live dashboard tour from Help if you want the screen guide again (the tour is shorter than the full manual).',
    'support_s5' => 'Send a support request with a topic, a subject, and full details, including order or withdrawal numbers.',
    'support_s6' => 'Attach screenshots or PDFs when the problem is on screen or about a payment.',
    'support_s7' => 'Follow the request status until it is solved, and send more proof if asked.',
    'support_s8' => 'Staff: work through the support request list, update the status, and close each one with a clear answer.',
    'support_summary' => 'Search this manual, restart the dashboard tour, and send support requests you can track.',
    'support_t1' => 'Search with Bangla or English words; many chapters can be found with both.',
    'support_t2' => 'Send one problem per request so it reaches the right person faster.',
    'support_title' => 'Help, user manual, and support requests',
    'support_w1' => 'Do not write passwords or full NID numbers in a support request.',
    'support_why' => 'Support only through Facebook or WhatsApp loses proof and has no promised reply time.',
    'website_customization_badge' => 'Website settings',
    'website_customization_o1' => 'The public website shows current offers and what is in stock.',
    'website_customization_o2' => 'Enquiries go into a list that can be followed up.',
    'website_customization_o3' => 'A clean, good-looking website helps bring in new dealers.',
    'website_customization_purpose' => 'The public website shows the brand and brings in new dealers. The panels handle the daily business work.',
    'website_customization_s1' => 'Open Website & training → Website design to change the banners and public text, where allowed.',
    'website_customization_s2' => 'Feature only products that are really in stock.',
    'website_customization_s3' => 'Publish content and circulars for rules and campaigns.',
    'website_customization_s4' => 'Sort enquiries and reply on time.',
    'website_customization_s5' => 'Move partnership applications into account joining.',
    'website_customization_s6' => 'Check on mobile and computer before publishing.',
    'website_customization_s7' => 'Keep the map and contact details correct for the Pirganj office unless the company says otherwise.',
    'website_customization_s8' => 'When testing public pages, check both the day and night themes.',
    'website_customization_s9' => 'Upload images and videos within the size and file type limits.',
    'website_customization_summary' => 'Manage how products, notices, and incoming enquiries appear on the public website.',
    'website_customization_t1' => 'Use the official brand logos and images every time.',
    'website_customization_t2' => 'Do not post requests for money on public pages.',
    'website_customization_title' => 'Public website, content, enquiries, and partnership applications',
    'website_customization_w1' => 'Do not show staff-only links in public menus.',
    'website_customization_why' => 'Old banners and unanswered enquiries cost you dealers and customer trust.',
    'withdrawals_badge' => 'Withdrawals & wallet',
    'withdrawals_o1' => 'You ask only for money that is available.',
    'withdrawals_o2' => 'Staff see a clear request with the receiving account and amount.',
    'withdrawals_o3' => 'Every paid withdrawal has a receipt you can check.',
    'withdrawals_purpose' => 'Withdrawals send money from your available wallet balance through an approval process, with receipts and tax papers where needed.',
    'withdrawals_s1' => 'Check that your available earnings are at least the company\'s minimum withdrawal amount.',
    'withdrawals_s10' => 'Keep your own tax records. Tax (TDS) or tax cut notes may show on receipts as per company rules.',
    'withdrawals_s2' => 'Finish any steps the system asks for first (often a past order or earnings) before the form opens.',
    'withdrawals_s3' => 'Choose how to receive the money and enter the correct account or wallet number, in the same name as your NID where required.',
    'withdrawals_s4' => 'Send the withdrawal request and note down the reference number.',
    'withdrawals_s5' => 'Follow the status: Pending → Approved/In review → Paid/Rejected.',
    'withdrawals_s6' => 'Download or open the receipt or statement when staff mark it paid.',
    'withdrawals_s7' => 'Staff: handle requests from Partner money → Withdrawal requests, with a second person checking.',
    'withdrawals_s8' => 'Owners: check unusual receiving accounts and sudden jumps in requests before pushing a payment through.',
    'withdrawals_s9' => 'If rejected, read the reason, fix your profile or account details, and send the request again only once.',
    'withdrawals_summary' => 'Withdraw your available earnings to Bank, bKash, Nagad, or Rocket, and follow the payment.',
    'withdrawals_t1' => 'After changing your account details, try a small withdrawal first.',
    'withdrawals_t2' => 'Plan around the payment days given in company circulars.',
    'withdrawals_t3' => 'If you also have staff access, withdraw from your dealer dashboard, not the staff one.',
    'withdrawals_title' => 'Withdrawals and where to receive money',
    'withdrawals_w1' => 'Never pay a “processing fee” to anyone who says they can speed up Madina payments.',
    'withdrawals_w2' => 'Do not share wallet OTPs with anyone who says they are from accounts.',
    'withdrawals_why' => 'Asking for more than your available balance, less than the minimum, or with wrong account details leads to rejection and delay.',
    'payment_receipts_badge' => 'Payment receipts',
    'payment_receipts_title' => 'Payment receipts: proof of every payout',
    'payment_receipts_summary' => 'Every time the office pays you by hand, a numbered receipt is made. See and print all of yours in one place.',
    'payment_receipts_purpose' => 'The office pays by hand for now. The receipt shows how much was paid, how (cash, bank, bKash, Nagad or other), the reference, the date and who paid.',
    'payment_receipts_why' => 'A receipt protects both you and the company: if there is ever a question about a payment, the receipt number and reference settle it quickly.',
    'payment_receipts_s1' => 'Open My money and press the Payment receipts tab.',
    'payment_receipts_s2' => 'Each row is one payment: receipt number (MN-PR-…), date, what it was for, method, reference and the amount paid.',
    'payment_receipts_s3' => 'Press View / print to open the receipt.',
    'payment_receipts_s4' => 'Choose Print (A4) for normal paper, or Print (small 80 mm) for a receipt printer. You can also save it as PDF from the print window.',
    'payment_receipts_s5' => 'Check that the amount, method and the last 4 digits of your account or wallet are right.',
    'payment_receipts_s6' => 'Staff: the receipt is made when you mark a withdrawal or a fund payment as paid. Choose the method and fill in the reference, the bank or wallet details, or for cash the name of the person who took it.',
    'payment_receipts_o1' => 'You have a printable receipt for every payment the office made to you.',
    'payment_receipts_o2' => 'You only ever see your own receipts.',
    'payment_receipts_t1' => 'When the office pays you a bike, car or tour reward, ask for the receipt number and keep it.',
    'payment_receipts_t2' => 'Keep the receipt number when you call the office about a payment.',
    'payment_receipts_w1' => 'If a receipt shows money you did not get, tell the office at once and give the receipt number.',
    'money_rules_badge' => 'Money rules',
    'money_rules_title' => 'Where your money comes from, and how each month closes',
    'money_rules_summary' => 'A short list of every commission, who gets it, and what happens to money at the end of each month.',
    'money_rules_purpose' => 'From every purchase, :dealer_fund_rate% (dealer purchase) or :sub_fund_rate% (sub-dealer purchase) goes to partners and funds. The rates below come from the live commission settings.',
    'money_rules_why' => 'When you know which money is paid at once, which waits for month end, and which needs a target, there are no surprises.',
    'money_rules_s1' => 'Only purchases that are fully paid and delivered count.',
    'money_rules_s2' => 'Cashback: the buyer gets :cashback_rate% of their own purchase back.',
    'money_rules_s3' => 'Referral: :referral_rate% to the person who referred the buyer, then :gen2_rate% and :gen3_rate% to the two people above them.',
    'money_rules_s4' => 'Area commission: :area_rate% shared among the area dealers of the buyer\'s place codes (management :area_management%, division :area_division%, district :area_district%, upazila :area_upazila%, Union / Pourashava :area_union%).',
    'money_rules_s5' => 'Dealer salary: :dealer_salary_rate% goes into the salary fund of the buyer\'s division. Dealers there who buy at least :dealer_salary_min that month share it equally.',
    'money_rules_s6' => 'Rank royalty: :royalty_rate% is shared each month among dealers who keep their rank. You get it only for your latest rank.',
    'money_rules_s7' => 'Rank award: :incentive_rate% builds the award fund. The one-time award is paid as soon as you reach a rank. Reaching MO and AM in the same month pays both.',
    'money_rules_s8' => 'Marketing (:marketing_rate%) and bike/car rewards (:vehicle_rate%) are company funds for campaigns and big rewards.',
    'money_rules_s9' => 'Each month closes on its own. If you miss a target (salary, area commission, royalty and so on), that month\'s money goes to the company profit fund, and the reason is recorded. It does not move to the next month.',
    'money_rules_s10' => 'Only three funds carry over from month to month: the rank award fund, the sub-dealer tour fund and the bike/car fund.',
    'money_rules_o1' => 'You can tell which money is paid at once and which waits for month end.',
    'money_rules_o2' => 'You know that a missed target means that month\'s share is lost, not saved for later.',
    'money_rules_t1' => 'Press “See my progress” on the Dashboard to see how close you are to each monthly target.',
    'money_rules_t2' => 'If the owner changes a rate, this page shows the new rate right away.',
    'money_rules_w1' => 'Do not wait for next month to make up a missed target. Each month is counted on its own.',
    'my_progress_badge' => 'My progress',
    'my_progress_title' => 'See my progress: salary, rank and rewards in one window',
    'my_progress_summary' => 'One button on your Dashboard shows how close you are to this month\'s salary, your next rank and the bike and car rewards.',
    'my_progress_purpose' => 'The progress window shows your targets for this month in simple bars, so you know what to buy and by when.',
    'my_progress_why' => 'Targets reset every month. Checking your progress early gives you time to reach them.',
    'my_progress_s1' => 'On the Dashboard, find the Targets box and press “See my progress”.',
    'my_progress_s2' => 'The top line shows this month\'s dates and how many days are left.',
    'my_progress_s3' => 'Monthly salary: dealers see how much more to buy to get this month\'s salary. Sub-dealers see the salary earned so far.',
    'my_progress_s4' => 'Rank and rank award (dealers): your rank now, the next rank, what is still needed, and your one-time award.',
    'my_progress_s5' => 'Keep your royalty: how much you must buy this month to get your rank\'s royalty.',
    'my_progress_s6' => 'Bike and car rewards: your team\'s total sales against each target.',
    'my_progress_s7' => 'Press Done to close it. The numbers are fresh each time you open the window.',
    'my_progress_o1' => 'You know exactly how much more to buy this month, and by which date.',
    'my_progress_o2' => 'You can see if your rank award is paid or still waiting.',
    'my_progress_t1' => 'Only orders that are paid and delivered count. An order waiting for payment check does not count yet.',
    'my_progress_t2' => 'Open it again near the end of the month before you place your last order.',
    'my_progress_w1' => 'The salary amount shown is an estimate. The final amount is paid after the month closes.',
    'office_chat_badge' => 'Chat with the office',
    'office_chat_title' => 'Messages between partners and the office',
    'office_chat_summary' => 'Partners send messages and photos to the office. The owner chooses which staff answer.',
    'office_chat_purpose' => 'Chat keeps every question and answer in the panel, so nothing is lost in personal phones.',
    'office_chat_why' => 'When the right staff answer, partners get help faster and the owner can see every chat.',
    'office_chat_s1' => 'Dealers and sub-dealers: open Contact the office → Message the office.',
    'office_chat_s2' => 'Type your message. You can add a photo, for example a payment screenshot.',
    'office_chat_s3' => 'Staff: if the owner chose you, open Partner messages to read and answer.',
    'office_chat_s4' => 'Owner: open Partner messages and then “Who answers partner chat”.',
    'office_chat_s5' => 'For each staff member choose No, Own branches only, or Whole company, then press Save. “Own branches only” means they see chats only from partners of their own branches.',
    'office_chat_s6' => 'Owners always see every chat.',
    'office_chat_o1' => 'Every partner question has a written answer in the panel.',
    'office_chat_o2' => 'Only the staff the owner chose can read partner chats.',
    'office_chat_t1' => 'Give the order number in your message so staff can find it fast.',
    'office_chat_t2' => 'For a problem that needs a proper record, send a support request too.',
    'office_chat_w1' => 'Never send your password or OTP in chat.',
    'data_cleanup_badge' => 'Data cleanup',
    'data_cleanup_title' => 'Data cleanup: deleting old records you no longer need',
    'data_cleanup_summary' => 'The owner can delete old login codes, SMS records and closed enquiries. Nothing is deleted on its own.',
    'data_cleanup_purpose' => 'Old login codes and SMS records pile up. The owner can clear them by hand. Orders, payments, accounts, commissions and the activity log are never shown here and can never be deleted here.',
    'data_cleanup_why' => 'Clearing old records keeps lists short. Making the owner choose each one keeps important data safe.',
    'data_cleanup_s1' => 'In the owner panel, open Data cleanup.',
    'data_cleanup_s2' => 'Choose the kind: Old login codes, SMS records or Closed enquiries.',
    'data_cleanup_s3' => 'Choose “Older than (days)” and press Show.',
    'data_cleanup_s4' => 'Tick the records to delete, or “Select all on this page”.',
    'data_cleanup_s5' => 'Press Delete selected and confirm. Deleted records cannot be brought back.',
    'data_cleanup_o1' => 'Old records you chose are gone for good.',
    'data_cleanup_o2' => 'Business records stay safe, because they never appear on this page.',
    'data_cleanup_t1' => 'Keep at least a few weeks of SMS records in case a partner asks about a message.',
    'data_cleanup_t2' => 'Only the owner can see this page. Staff cannot.',
    'data_cleanup_w1' => 'Deleting cannot be undone. Check the list before you press Delete.',

    'courier_ordering_badge' => 'Courier',
    'courier_ordering_title' => 'Choosing a courier and following your parcel',
    'courier_ordering_summary' => 'Pick a courier when you order, or let the company decide. Then follow the parcel on the order page.',
    'courier_ordering_purpose' => 'The order form has a “Courier” box. It lists the couriers the owner has switched on, and “Company decides”.',
    'courier_ordering_why' => 'You can pick the courier that works best in your area, and see where your parcel is without calling anyone.',
    'courier_ordering_s1' => 'Open “New order” and make your order as usual.',
    'courier_ordering_s2' => 'In the “Courier” box, pick a courier. If any courier is fine, leave it on “Company decides”.',
    'courier_ordering_s3' => 'If you picked a courier, the parcel is booked with that courier by itself once your order is approved.',
    'courier_ordering_s4' => 'If you left it on “Company decides”, the office chooses the courier and sends the parcel.',
    'courier_ordering_s5' => 'Open the order. Under “Parcel tracking” you can see the step: Waiting for pickup, Picked up, On the way, Delivered. A parcel sent back shows “Returned”.',
    'courier_ordering_s6' => 'Press “Copy” to copy the tracking number. Press “Track on the courier website” to open the courier\'s own page.',
    'courier_ordering_s7' => 'If the office changes your courier, you get a notice. The order page shows the change and any note from the office.',
    'courier_ordering_o1' => 'You know which courier has your parcel and what the tracking number is.',
    'courier_ordering_o2' => 'You get a notice on the bell each time the parcel moves to a new step.',
    'courier_ordering_t1' => 'The system asks the courier for news every 30 minutes, and also when the order page is opened.',
    'courier_ordering_t2' => 'Give the tracking number to the person who will receive the parcel.',
    'courier_ordering_w1' => 'When the courier says “Delivered”, the order is still not finished. The office must confirm the delivery first. Commission comes only after that.',

    'courier_staff_badge' => 'Courier',
    'courier_staff_title' => 'Automatic booking and changing the courier',
    'courier_staff_summary' => 'When a dealer picks a courier, the parcel is booked by itself on approval. Staff can change the courier and leave a note.',
    'courier_staff_purpose' => 'An order with a chosen courier does not need a hand dispatch. A “Company decides” order is still dispatched by hand.',
    'courier_staff_why' => 'Automatic booking saves typing, and the dealer gets the tracking number sooner. The note tells the dealer why the courier changed.',
    'courier_staff_s1' => 'Owner: switch on the couriers in “SMS & courier setup”. Dealers can pick only those.',
    'courier_staff_s2' => 'Approve the order as usual. If the dealer picked a courier, stock comes out of the branch and the parcel is booked with that courier by itself.',
    'courier_staff_s3' => 'The goods come from the head office, unless another branch was chosen for the order.',
    'courier_staff_s4' => 'If the courier is switched off, no active branch holds stock, or the branch is short of stock, nothing is sent. You get a bell notice. Change the courier or dispatch by hand.',
    'courier_staff_s5' => 'For a “Company decides” order, open the order and use the dispatch form. Pick a courier under “Book with a courier (optional)”, or type the courier name and tracking number.',
    'courier_staff_s6' => 'To change the courier, open the order and go to “Change courier”. Pick the “New courier”, add a note for the dealer if you want, and press “Change courier”.',
    'courier_staff_s7' => 'If the courier has collected the parcel but the step has not moved, press “Mark picked up”.',
    'courier_staff_s8' => 'When the goods have really arrived, press “Confirm delivery”. The courier saying “Delivered” does not finish the order.',
    'courier_staff_o1' => 'The dealer gets a notice. If you wrote a note, the dealer sees it too.',
    'courier_staff_o2' => 'The order history keeps every courier change.',
    'courier_staff_t1' => 'You can change the courier only before the booking is made, or after the courier refused it.',
    'courier_staff_t2' => 'These buttons are for staff who handle orders or stock. Nobody can use them on their own order.',
    'courier_staff_w1' => 'Approval books the parcel straight away. Check the order carefully before you approve it.',

    'deliveries_board_badge' => 'Deliveries',
    'deliveries_board_title' => 'The deliveries board and failed bookings',
    'deliveries_board_summary' => 'The Deliveries page lists every courier parcel and every booking the courier refused.',
    'deliveries_board_purpose' => 'Staff and the owner use this page to see where each parcel is and to fix refused bookings.',
    'deliveries_board_why' => 'A refused booking means the parcel has not left. This list keeps those orders in front of you.',
    'deliveries_board_s1' => 'Open “Orders & delivery” → “Deliveries”.',
    'deliveries_board_s2' => '“Failed bookings” is at the top. The courier did not accept these parcels. The “Problem” column says why.',
    'deliveries_board_s3' => 'Press the order number to open the order. Then press “Try booking again”, or use “Change courier”.',
    'deliveries_board_s4' => '“Courier parcels” lists every parcel booked with a courier. Choose a “Step” or a “Courier” and press “Show”.',
    'deliveries_board_s5' => 'Press a tracking number to open the courier\'s own page.',
    'deliveries_board_s6' => 'The page shows the branch picked in the top bar.',
    'deliveries_board_o1' => 'You can see how many parcels are at each step.',
    'deliveries_board_o2' => 'A failed booking leaves the list once it is booked.',
    'deliveries_board_t1' => 'You also get a bell notice when a booking fails.',
    'deliveries_board_w1' => 'If the “Problem” column says the courier gave no clear answer, the parcel may already be booked. Check the courier\'s own panel first. If it is there, do not book it again.',

    'notification_panel_badge' => 'Notifications',
    'notification_panel_title' => 'The bell and the notification panel',
    'notification_panel_summary' => 'Press the bell in the top bar to read your newest notices from any page.',
    'notification_panel_purpose' => 'The bell shows your 15 newest notices. A number on it tells you how many are unread.',
    'notification_panel_why' => 'You see order, payment and company news quickly, without leaving the page you are on.',
    'notification_panel_s1' => 'Look at the bell in the top bar. A number on it means you have unread notices.',
    'notification_panel_s2' => 'Press the bell. On a computer a small panel opens. On a phone it covers the screen.',
    'notification_panel_s3' => 'Press a notice to open it. It then counts as read.',
    'notification_panel_s4' => 'Press “Mark all as read” to clear every unread notice at once.',
    'notification_panel_s5' => 'Press “See all notifications” at the bottom for the full list.',
    'notification_panel_s6' => 'To close it, press the X or anywhere outside the panel.',
    'notification_panel_o1' => 'The number on the bell goes down as you read.',
    'notification_panel_t1' => 'Order news, payment news and support replies all come here.',
    'notification_panel_w1' => 'Never give anyone your password or OTP, even if a message asks for it.',

    'branch_switcher_badge' => 'Branches',
    'branch_switcher_title' => 'Changing branch from the top bar',
    'branch_switcher_summary' => 'Pick a branch in the top bar and the office pages show only that branch.',
    'branch_switcher_purpose' => 'Office staff and the owner have a branch list in the top bar. Dealers and sub-dealers do not have it.',
    'branch_switcher_why' => 'You can look at one branch\'s work without mixing it with the others.',
    'branch_switcher_s1' => 'Press the branch name in the top bar. On a phone it is under the page title.',
    'branch_switcher_s2' => 'The owner, and staff who work with accounts, stock or finance, see every branch and also “All branches”.',
    'branch_switcher_s3' => 'Other staff see only the branches they are assigned to. They do not get “All branches”.',
    'branch_switcher_s4' => 'Staff with no branch do not get the list. Pages that follow the branch stay empty until the owner gives them one.',
    'branch_switcher_s5' => 'Pick a branch. Dashboard, Orders, Deliveries, Check order payments, Withdrawal requests, Reports, Top sellers, Dealer list, Sub-dealer list and Staff list then show that branch.',
    'branch_switcher_s6' => 'These pages say which branch you are looking at, for example “Showing: Head Office”.',
    'branch_switcher_o1' => 'You see the numbers for one branch at a time.',
    'branch_switcher_t1' => 'Check the branch name before you record stock or anything else for a branch.',
    'branch_switcher_w1' => 'Staff cannot open a branch they are not assigned to, even by typing its address.',

    'website_button_badge' => 'Website',
    'website_button_title' => 'The “Visit website” button',
    'website_button_summary' => 'The globe in the top bar opens the company\'s public website.',
    'website_button_purpose' => 'You can go from your panel to the public website with one press.',
    'website_button_why' => 'You can see product pages and company details the way customers see them.',
    'website_button_s1' => 'Press the globe in the top bar. Its name is “Visit website”.',
    'website_button_s2' => 'The public website opens in the same browser tab.',
    'website_button_s3' => 'To come back, press your browser\'s back button.',
    'website_button_s4' => 'The same link is in the menu under your photo.',
    'website_button_o1' => 'You see the website the way customers see it.',
    'website_button_t1' => 'To keep your panel open, open the website in a new browser tab.',
    'website_button_w1' => 'Going to the website does not log you out. On someone else\'s computer, log out when you finish.',

    'prescriptions_partner_badge' => 'Prescriptions',
    'prescriptions_partner_title' => 'Prescriptions for dealers and sub-dealers',
    'prescriptions_partner_summary' => 'Once your registration is checked, you can keep patients and write prescriptions.',
    'prescriptions_partner_purpose' => 'Prescriptions are off for every dealer and sub-dealer at first. The menu item appears only after your registration is checked and prescriptions are turned on.',
