    'global_search_s1' => 'Press Search in the top bar, or press Ctrl+K.',
    'global_search_s2' => 'Type at least 2 letters or numbers: an order number, name, code, phone or SKU.',
    'global_search_s3' => 'The results come in three groups: Orders, Partners and Products. Press one to open it.',
    'global_search_o1' => 'You reach the right order or partner in a few seconds.',
    'global_search_t1' => 'If nothing comes up, check the spelling or try a shorter word.',
    'global_search_w1' => 'You see only what your permission and branch allow. Phone numbers are always shown masked.',

    'company_funds_heads_badge' => 'Company funds',
    'company_funds_heads_title' => 'Company funds and expense heads',
    'company_funds_heads_summary' => 'See how much each fund holds, record money taken out, and see what it was spent on.',
    'company_funds_heads_purpose' => 'Company accounts → Company funds has four tabs: Funds, Waiting for approval, Expense heads and Spending report.',
    'company_funds_heads_why' => 'Every taka taken out has a head, a payee and a reference, so you can always say where it went.',
    'company_funds_heads_s1' => 'On the Funds tab each fund shows money in, money out, what is waiting for approval and the balance now. Press “See history” for the details.',
    'company_funds_heads_s2' => 'To record a spend, press “Take money out” on the fund. Fill in the expense head, amount, date, who was paid, how it was paid and the reference. A receipt is optional.',
    'company_funds_heads_s3' => 'Press “Send for approval”. The money leaves the fund only when the spend is approved. If it is rejected, the money stays in the fund.',
    'company_funds_heads_s4' => 'On the Expense heads tab, add a head in English and Bangla, change it, or switch it off.',
    'company_funds_heads_s5' => 'The Sub-dealer tour fund can use only heads marked “For company tours”.',
    'company_funds_heads_s6' => 'The Car and bike award fund, Rank award reserve and Salary reserve are paid only through their own award rules, so they cannot be spent here.',
    'company_funds_heads_s7' => 'On the Spending report tab, choose dates, a fund or a head and press Show. Press “Download Excel” to save it.',
    'company_funds_heads_o1' => 'Every spend shows its fund, head, amount, payee and reference.',
    'company_funds_heads_t1' => 'The same spending report is also in Reports → Report Centre.',
    'company_funds_heads_w1' => 'A fund cannot spend more than it holds, and a reference can be used only once. No partner can withdraw or move tour fund money.',

    'accounting_statements_badge' => 'Accounting',
    'accounting_statements_title' => 'Accounting statements: what they show and what they do not',
    'accounting_statements_summary' => 'Trial balance, profit and loss, and balance sheet from the money journal. They are not a full set of accounts yet.',
    'accounting_statements_purpose' => 'These statements use only the journal. The journal holds commissions, payroll, payouts, opening balances and clinic sales. Product sales and purchase costs are not in it.',
    'accounting_statements_why' => 'Because sales and purchases are missing, the “Result for the period” is not the company\'s profit.',
    'accounting_statements_s1' => 'Open Company accounts → Accounting. Stay on the Statements tab.',
    'accounting_statements_s2' => 'Choose the From and To dates and press Show.',
    'accounting_statements_s3' => 'Read Trial balance, Profit and loss, and Balance sheet.',
    'accounting_statements_s4' => 'Read the “Check against the journal” box. It says whether the statements match the journal.',
    'accounting_statements_s5' => 'Press Excel or PDF to download.',
    'accounting_statements_o1' => 'You can see commissions, salaries, payouts and clinic sales for any dates.',
    'accounting_statements_t1' => 'If the screen says the statements do not match or the journal does not balance, tell the technical team before using the figures.',
    'accounting_statements_w1' => 'This is not a full set of accounts yet, because sales and purchases are not in the journal. Do not use it as the company\'s full profit or as audited statements.',

    'statement_matching_badge' => 'Statement check',
    'statement_matching_title' => 'Matching a bank, bKash or Nagad statement',
    'statement_matching_summary' => 'Upload a statement and the system suggests which pending payment claims match it.',
    'statement_matching_purpose' => 'The Statement check tab on Company accounts → Accounting saves the time of checking each line by eye. Staff still decide.',
    'statement_matching_why' => 'A reference used twice or an amount that differs is easy to miss on paper. The system points them out.',
